(6779809, 1016494, 57229, '<td valign="top"><a href="//masters-of-photography.com/A/adams/adams_aspens_full.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">why not?</a>, indeed<br/>another time of day, maybe, (and having all the time in the world to mess about with it) or another extra long exposure thrown in there (if you''re using multiple exposure HDR), could bring out some depth in the woods. That''s only if your really, really want to copy the AA original, of course. It''s arguably better with the light on the edge and the mystery behind...</td>', 'why not?, indeedanother time of day, maybe, (and having all the time in the world to mess about with it) or another extra long exposure thrown in there (if you''re using multiple exposure HDR), could bring out some depth in the woods. That''s only if your really, really want to copy the AA original, of course. It''s arguably better with the light on the edge and the mystery behind...', '2012-05-28 06:01:51.000000', NULL, 0),
